\name{LatticeDotLayerProcessor}
\alias{LatticeDotLayerProcessor}
\title{lattice Dot Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads a \code{dotplot()} panel that has at most one value per level -- a
Cleveland dot plot -- as a \code{dot} layer, which the frontend builds on its
bar reading: one value per category, walked along the axis. One layer
per group, named after it.

The panel's rows were sorted by level before drawing
(\code{\link[=lattice_prepare]{lattice_prepare()}}), so the dots are drawn in the order the levels run
along the axis, which is the order the frontend pairs a bar-shaped
layer's marks with its values.
}
\keyword{internal}
